## Works in conjunction with team data from teams.ftl

## index.html.hbs
funding-page-title = Funding
funding-intro = Rust depends on hundreds of contributors who improve it on a daily basis, many of whom are volunteers. We want them to be properly supported to ensure the long-term health of the Rust Project. We are very grateful for any financial contributions that go towards supporting the development and maintenance of Rust. This page describes several ways how you can support Rust contributors.<br /><br />
    If your company would like to discuss how it could financially support Rust, please reach out the <a href="mailto:funding@rust-lang.org">Funding team</a>.
funding-maintenance-title = Fund maintenance
funding-rfmf-description = Continuous <a href="https://blog.rust-lang.org/inside-rust/2026/01/12/what-is-maintenance-anyway/">maintenance</a> is crucial to ensure that the Rust toolchain will be working correctly long-term and will be able to evolve without facing insurmountable technical debt. The Rust Foundation Maintainers Fund collects donations used to provide stable funding for contributors who maintain critical areas of the Rust toolchain. This program is managed by the <a href="{ $funding-team-url }">Funding team</a>, which communicates both with Rust teams and sponsors and selects the funded <a href="{ $mir-url }">Maintainers in Residence</a>.<br /><br />
    Contribute to this fund if you want to let us choose where your money will benefit the development and maintenance of Rust the most.
funding-rfmf-donate = Donate to the Maintainer Fund
funding-rfmf-mir-link = View funded maintainers
funding-features-title = Fund features and improvements
funding-features-description = <a href="https://goals.rust-lang.org">Rust Project Goals</a> track various initiatives to add new features or make improvements to the Rust language and its toolchain. Some of those Goals require funding, to allow the contributors to dedicate time and focus for working on the improvement.<br /><br />
    Fund Project Goals if your company wants to help push forward specific initiatives to improve Rust.
funding-goals-link = View Goals looking for funding
funding-sponsors-title = Sponsor individual contributors
funding-sponsors-description = Several Rust Project contributors have their own personal GitHub Sponsors account. If you want to sponsor specific individuals who work on Rust, you can do so below.

## mir.html.hbs
mir-page-title = Maintainers in Residence
mir-intro = The Rust Foundation Maintainers Fund (RFMF) funds Rust Project contributors who maintain important parts of the Rust toolchain through the <a href="https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/3931-rfmf-rust-foundation-maintainer-fund.html">Maintainer in Residence</a> (MiR) program. This page lists contributors who are currently funded by RFMF. <br /><br />Read more about how you can help financially support our contributors <a href="{ $funding-url }">here</a>.
mir-title = Maintainer in Residence
mir-description = These contributors work as full-time or part-time Maintainers in Residence in the Rust Project.
mir-grant-title = Maintainer grant
mir-grant-description = These contributors are supported with a small monthly grant to fund their Rust maintenance work.
